<% pageTitle = "Our Story — Kachhomal Sweets" %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Our story</span>
    <h1>Seven decades, one counter.</h1>
    <p>Kachhomal has been part of Ulhasnagar's everyday life since 1952 — through weddings, festivals, and quiet Tuesday evenings when someone just wanted a piece of barfi.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it began</span>
      <h2>Built by hand, one batch at a time.</h2>
      <p>Kachhomal was founded in 1952 by a family that had just rebuilt its life in Ulhasnagar. With little more than a stove, a few brass vessels and a recipe carried from home, the first counter sold laddu and barfi to a neighbourhood that was rebuilding itself too.</p>
      <p>What kept people coming back wasn't marketing — it was consistency. The same ghee, the same hand-rolled process, the same shop, visit after visit, year after year.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split-media reveal">
      <img src="/images/heritage-shop.jpg" alt="Vintage-style photo of an old Indian sweet shop storefront" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Milestones</span>
      <h2>A short, honest timeline.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="timeline reveal">
      <li>
        <span class="year">1952</span>
        <div>
          <h4>The first counter opens</h4>
          <p>A single shop near Siru Chowk begins selling fresh laddu and barfi to the local community.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="year">1970s–80s</span>
        <div>
          <h4>The menu grows</h4>
          <p>Kaju katli, motichoor laddu and namkeen join the counter as demand for festival and wedding orders increases.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="year">1990s–2000s</span>
        <div>
          <h4>New outlets across Ulhasnagar</h4>
          <p>As the next generation joins the business, additional counters open across Ulhasnagar No. 1, 2 and Camp 5.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="year">Today</span>
        <div>
          <h4>Still weighed by hand</h4>
          <p>Every box is still packed and weighed at the counter — now backed by online ordering for festivals, weddings and gifting.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">What we believe</span>
      <h2>Three things we've never compromised on.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div class="card reveal">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Fresh, not stocked</h3>
          <p>Everything is made in small batches through the day — nothing is prepared days in advance and held in storage.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>Pure ingredients</h3>
          <p>Ghee, khoya and dry fruits are sourced and checked before every batch — no shortcuts, especially during festival season.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>The counter still matters</h3>
          <p>Even as we go online, every order is still packed by hand by people who've been doing this for years.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
